WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.201 --> 00:00:02.635
-Moving on,
we here at "Late Night"

00:00:02.635 --> 00:00:06.139
don't always have enough time
to cover all of the recent news.

00:00:06.139 --> 00:00:07.906
So here with a recap
is one of our writers,

00:00:07.906 --> 00:00:11.344
Amber Ruffin, in a segment
we call "Amber Says What."

00:00:11.344 --> 00:00:14.247
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:14.247 --> 00:00:15.381
-Hey.

00:00:15.381 --> 00:00:18.751
You guys,
things have been crazy.

00:00:18.751 --> 00:00:20.186
Okay, first of all,

00:00:20.186 --> 00:00:24.090
I heard 80-year-old actor
Robert De Niro just had a child,

00:00:24.090 --> 00:00:25.658
and I was like, "What?"

00:00:25.658 --> 00:00:30.129
Then I heard 83-year-old
Al Pacino also just had a child,

00:00:30.129 --> 00:00:31.664
and I was like, "What?"

00:00:31.664 --> 00:00:35.301
What old man is going
to have a toddler next, Seth?

00:00:35.301 --> 00:00:37.770
[ Laughter ]

00:00:37.770 --> 00:00:40.974
-I do have a toddler.
-Gross. How?

00:00:40.974 --> 00:00:42.541
-The normal way.

00:00:42.541 --> 00:00:44.477
-Ew!

00:00:44.477 --> 00:00:46.078
-Why don't you have a child?

00:00:46.078 --> 00:00:47.947
-Because I am a child.

00:00:47.947 --> 00:00:49.849
A sexy little child.

00:00:49.849 --> 00:00:51.484
[ Tink! ]

00:00:51.484 --> 00:00:54.420
Then I heard that
they arrested Tupac's killer,

00:00:54.420 --> 00:00:58.091
and I was like, "What...
is next on your to-do list?

00:00:58.091 --> 00:01:00.493
Get a warrant
for John Wilkes Booth?"

00:01:00.493 --> 00:01:02.061
You're late!

00:01:02.061 --> 00:01:04.764
Why not figure out
who shot J.R.?

00:01:04.764 --> 00:01:06.966
-Oh, it was Kristin Shepard.

00:01:06.966 --> 00:01:09.135
-You are so old.

00:01:09.135 --> 00:01:12.272
-I'm only five years
older than you.

00:01:12.272 --> 00:01:14.673
-I don't like this anymore.

00:01:14.673 --> 00:01:18.411
Then I heard that Ron DeSantis
wears secret high-heeled boots,

00:01:18.411 --> 00:01:20.813
and I was like, "Wh-ha-ha-at?"

00:01:20.813 --> 00:01:25.451
You must hate being short more
than you hate drag queens.

00:01:25.451 --> 00:01:27.987
Speaking of drag queens,
with those high heels,

00:01:27.987 --> 00:01:29.322
you are one sew-in away

00:01:29.322 --> 00:01:32.825
from violating
your own anti-trans bill, honey.

00:01:32.825 --> 00:01:36.696
Then I read that all of
Trump's kids are testifying,

00:01:36.696 --> 00:01:38.931
and I was like, "What?!"

00:01:38.931 --> 00:01:42.202
Ivanka, Don Jr., Eric.

00:01:44.003 --> 00:01:46.172
All the kids.

00:01:46.172 --> 00:01:48.875
Man, I think
he might go to jail.

00:01:48.875 --> 00:01:51.577
Now, I know, I know,
he may be rich,

00:01:51.577 --> 00:01:54.414
he may be old,
and he may be a white man,

00:01:54.414 --> 00:01:57.317
but -- oops, never mind,
he will never go to jail.

00:01:57.317 --> 00:02:00.319
He'll probably just do what all
the other old guys are doing --

00:02:00.319 --> 00:02:05.324
have a baby, which I believe
to be a prison in its own right.

00:02:05.324 --> 00:02:07.627
Okay, so then I heard En Vogue

00:02:07.627 --> 00:02:11.163
is going to be in the
Macy's Thanksgiving Day Parade.

00:02:11.163 --> 00:02:14.300
I was like, "What?!"
And I have to say this.

00:02:14.300 --> 00:02:17.169
Please, NBC, corporate daddy,

00:02:17.169 --> 00:02:20.473
you have to let me in
to see that.

00:02:20.473 --> 00:02:23.809
Oh, Seth, do you have tickets
to the parade?

00:02:23.809 --> 00:02:24.910
-No.

00:02:24.910 --> 00:02:27.246
-Then what is the point of you?

00:02:27.246 --> 00:02:28.748
Why are we doing this?

00:02:28.748 --> 00:02:30.483
What is any of this for

00:02:30.483 --> 00:02:33.385
if it's not going to help us
see En Vogue?

00:02:33.385 --> 00:02:35.888
Then Britney Spears
released her memoir,

00:02:35.888 --> 00:02:39.125
"The Woman in Me," and spilled
the tea on Justin Timberlake.

00:02:39.125 --> 00:02:41.160
And I was like, "Wh-ha-aaaat?"

00:02:41.160 --> 00:02:42.628
It's, like, a lot,

00:02:42.628 --> 00:02:45.464
and I don't know if I'm allowed
to talk about what she said,

00:02:45.464 --> 00:02:47.934
but let's just say this.

00:02:55.474 --> 00:02:57.676
Now, do you want to hear
some more gossip?

00:02:57.676 --> 00:03:00.446
Okay, so,
Congressman George Santos

00:03:00.446 --> 00:03:03.783
was running around his job
with a baby,

00:03:03.783 --> 00:03:05.584
and I was like, "What?"

00:03:05.584 --> 00:03:10.723
When asked if the baby was his,
he said, "Not yet."

00:03:10.723 --> 00:03:13.126
[ Laughter ]

00:03:13.126 --> 00:03:17.530
Which brings us to a segment
called "Amber Says Why."

00:03:17.530 --> 00:03:21.033
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:21.033 --> 00:03:25.637
Now, George Santos said
this baby wasn't his yet.

00:03:25.637 --> 00:03:30.275
Why? Yet? Is that a threat?
And if so, to who?

00:03:30.275 --> 00:03:32.077
To me? America?

00:03:32.077 --> 00:03:34.714
Whoever's baby that is?
What?

00:03:34.714 --> 00:03:37.316
Whose baby is that and why?

00:03:37.316 --> 00:03:39.018
Why the baby, George?

00:03:39.018 --> 00:03:40.920
Why did they give
their baby to you?

00:03:40.920 --> 00:03:43.455
Did you trick somebody
and steal their baby?

00:03:43.455 --> 00:03:44.857
Where did you get
that baby from?

00:03:44.857 --> 00:03:48.060
Does it want to go back?
Did you ever give the baby back?

00:03:48.060 --> 00:03:51.163
Why the baby, George?
For what reason?

00:03:51.163 --> 00:03:53.566
What purpose was the baby
supposed to serve?

00:03:53.566 --> 00:03:55.501
And did it serve that purpose?

00:03:55.501 --> 00:03:58.504
And why does that baby
look more qualified

00:03:58.504 --> 00:04:01.040
to work in Congress than you?

00:04:01.040 --> 00:04:03.009
This has been "Amber Says Why."

00:04:03.009 --> 00:04:05.311
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:06.679 --> 00:04:10.116
Then I read that Beyoncé's
"Renaissance" tour

00:04:10.116 --> 00:04:13.352
made $579 million.

00:04:13.352 --> 00:04:14.554
[ Audience cheers ]

00:04:14.554 --> 00:04:15.654
Me too, man.

00:04:15.654 --> 00:04:17.089
It made so much money,

00:04:17.089 --> 00:04:20.459
it literally boosted the economy
everywhere it went.

00:04:20.459 --> 00:04:23.362
I read that and I was like...

00:04:23.362 --> 00:04:26.699
because I'm not about to mess up
the Beyoncé mute challenge.

00:04:26.699 --> 00:04:27.967
Mnh-mnh.

00:04:27.967 --> 00:04:30.102
Then I saw that Beyoncé
went to the premiere

00:04:30.102 --> 00:04:33.939
of Taylor Swift's new movie,
and I was like, "What?!"

00:04:33.939 --> 00:04:36.476
Beyoncé is not at
a Taylor Swift premiere.

00:04:36.476 --> 00:04:40.412
A Taylor Swift premiere
is at a Beyoncé.

00:04:40.412 --> 00:04:42.281
And I can't even imagine

00:04:42.281 --> 00:04:44.516
what Beyoncé in a movie theater
looks like.

00:04:44.516 --> 00:04:46.652
Walking up to
the concession stand like,

00:04:46.652 --> 00:04:50.956
"I will have the Sugar Babies
and a bottle of Cristal."

00:04:50.956 --> 00:04:52.325
Then --

00:04:52.325 --> 00:04:55.427
[ Laughter ]

00:04:55.427 --> 00:04:57.897
It came out so much worse.

00:04:59.531 --> 00:05:02.234
Then I heard there were
a million bedbugs in Paris,

00:05:02.234 --> 00:05:04.504
and I was like, "Quoi?"

00:05:04.504 --> 00:05:08.841
Then I found out Usher was doing
the Super Bowl halftime show,

00:05:08.841 --> 00:05:10.976
and I was like, "What!"

00:05:10.976 --> 00:05:13.579
Well, I guess I'm going to
have to cook him

00:05:13.579 --> 00:05:16.582
a real big breakfast
that morning.

00:05:16.582 --> 00:05:18.050
Not because
I'm sleeping with him,

00:05:18.050 --> 00:05:21.153
but because I had to take on
an extra job as Usher's cook

00:05:21.153 --> 00:05:24.257
'cause the writers' strike
lasted five months.

00:05:24.257 --> 00:05:26.359
Then I found out the actors
were still striking,

00:05:26.359 --> 00:05:28.527
and I was like, "What?"

00:05:28.527 --> 00:05:30.062
Matter of fact, Seth,

00:05:30.062 --> 00:05:32.632
how am I allowed to be
doing this right now?

00:05:32.632 --> 00:05:35.167
-Well, late-night television
shows fall under a specific --

00:05:35.167 --> 00:05:37.636
-Ohh! Shut up.

00:05:37.636 --> 00:05:41.106
Then I heard that genetic
testing company 23andMe

00:05:41.106 --> 00:05:44.377
was hacked, and I was like,
"What...were you thinking

00:05:44.377 --> 00:05:46.345
when you gave away all
your genetic information

00:05:46.345 --> 00:05:47.880
to some random company?"

00:05:47.880 --> 00:05:50.816
See, that's why
I never did 23andMe.

00:05:50.816 --> 00:05:53.486
Well, that and in case
I ever want to do a murder.

00:05:53.486 --> 00:05:55.687
I want to get away with it.

00:05:55.687 --> 00:05:57.957
Then I heard
Congresswoman Lauren Boebert

00:05:57.957 --> 00:05:59.992
got kicked out
of the musical "Beetlejuice"

00:05:59.992 --> 00:06:02.027
for getting felt up by some guy.

00:06:02.027 --> 00:06:03.929
And I was like, "What?!"

00:06:03.929 --> 00:06:06.632
"Beetlejuice"?
More like "Some Like It Hot."

00:06:09.368 --> 00:06:12.371 line:0%
"Some Like It Hot,"
co-written by Amber Ruffin,

00:06:12.371 --> 00:06:14.974 line:0%
now on Broadway
at the Shubert Theatre.

00:06:14.974 --> 00:06:18.010 line:0%
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:06:18.010 --> 00:06:21.513
Boebert, why would you guys
stay in your seats for that?

00:06:21.513 --> 00:06:23.148
At least escape to the bathroom

00:06:23.148 --> 00:06:25.050
and pretend
you're taking a whiz.

00:06:25.050 --> 00:06:28.120 line:0%
"The Wiz,"
written by Amber Ruffin,

00:06:28.120 --> 00:06:31.324 line:0%
touring America and coming
to Broadway March 29th.

00:06:31.324 --> 00:06:33.692 line:0%
Tickets available
at wizmusical.com.

00:06:33.692 --> 00:06:35.995 line:0%
-Hey, Amber, why do you
keep interrupting this bit

00:06:35.995 --> 00:06:37.663
to plug all
your Broadway musicals?

00:06:37.663 --> 00:06:40.232
-Because the strike
took too long,

00:06:40.232 --> 00:06:43.102
and I got to make money
to take care of this baby.

00:06:47.172 --> 00:06:49.908
-Amber, is that your baby?

00:06:49.908 --> 00:06:51.811
-Not yet.
[ Tink! ]

00:06:51.811 --> 00:06:53.612
This has been "Amber Says What."

00:06:53.612 --> 00:06:55.782
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:06:59.818 --> 00:07:00.953
-Amber Ruffin, everybody.

00:07:00.953 --> 00:07:03.256
We'll be right back
with Rachel Maddow.

